<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="263" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Per-customer Spaarke-tenant shared mailbox: provisioning creates, scopes and verifies it, and writes the stamp's sprk_communicationaccount row (#1562, owner decision 2026-10-10)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — mail (found by spaarke-auth-system-of-record-r1)</phase>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Exchange permissions, a new handler/sub-step, tenant isolation of mail.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Design decisions on Exchange RBAC and identity.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, exchange, tenant-isolation, security, testing</tags>
    <deps>none</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement the owner's mail model for Model 1: one Spaarke-tenant shared mailbox per customer, created and verified by provisioning.</prompt>

  <goal>A provisioned stamp has exactly one Spaarke-tenant shared mailbox for its customer, inside the stamp's Exchange scope group (so H14a's group-scoped Mail.* roles reach it and nothing else), with a verified `sprk_communicationaccount` row in the stamp's Dataverse — no hand steps.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner decision 2026-10-10 (#1562): one Spaarke-tenant shared mailbox per customer, created and verified by a provisioning
      step after H14a. Under Model 1 only Spaarke-tenant mailboxes are reachable (customer staff mailboxes live in their home
      tenant). Today `sprk_communicationaccount` rows are created by hand and no guide says so
      (`notes/coordination/2026-10-09-from-auth-system-of-record-r1-webhooks.md` §2). H14a grants the stamp identity
      Exchange-scoped Mail.Read/ReadWrite/Send scoped to the customer's mail-enabled security group (intake
      `exchangePolicyScopeGroupId`); the Worker reaches Exchange only through the H14a sidecar as `Spaarke Exchange Admin`
      (narrowed role `Spaarke App RBAC Admin`; widening it is an OWNER decision — `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md`).
      The BFF's GraphSubscriptionManager subscribes per receive-enabled account; `POST /api/communications/accounts/{id}/verify`
      verifies an account.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Never add a secret, certificate or Entra role to Spaarke Exchange Admin. If creating a shared mailbox needs a wider Exchange role, STOP that part and escalate with the narrowest Exchange role/scope that works (e.g. a custom management role with New-Mailbox -Shared and group membership only) — do not widen it yourself.</constraint>
    <constraint source="provisioning.md">The L2 main site runs no shell tool; Exchange only via the H14a sidecar contract. Idempotent read-then-write; one producer per input; validate intake at POST /api/runs with shared code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live">No live action. Tests only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Design note `notes/t263-customer-shared-mailbox.md`: naming (address/alias derived from customerId; display name from intake displayName), where it runs (new H14 sub-step after H14a, or H14a extension), the exact Exchange cmdlets and the minimum role they need (cite Microsoft Learn), membership in the scope group, idempotency, decommission, and the Dataverse `sprk_communicationaccount` row + BFF verify call (which identity, which endpoint). One recommendation; list any owner decision needed.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement what does not need an owner decision: sidecar contract + Worker sub-step, Dataverse row writer, H13 check that the account exists and is verified; tests incl. negative cases (mailbox exists outside the scope group, foreign mailbox name collision, verify fails).</step>
    <step order="3">Docs: deployment guide §7.9 mail section (replace the hand-made-rows text), prerequisites if any, defer-issues entry; propose `.claude/` edits verbatim.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A run creates (or adopts) exactly one shared mailbox for the customer, member of the scope group; a second run writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The stamp has one `sprk_communicationaccount` row for it, verified; H13 fails if missing or unverified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A same-named mailbox outside the scope group or owned by another customer quarantines the run (no change).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build 0/0; ControlPlane tests, ArchTests, LoadTests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
